      },
      {
        "global_revision": 3616,
        "object_type": "script",
        "object_id": "23984e5a-ecf5-491b-af97-176e2f29e69d",
        "object_revision": 5,
        "operation": "update",
        "created_at": "2026-10-17T04:16:58.881197385Z"
      }
    ],
    "explanation": "two owned script updates advanced the hub watermark by 2; the agent applies the new watermark on the change notification and reports it back via SYNC_ACK (row) or heartbeat (<=30s). A hub-side sample taken before the ack is exactly the number of intervening hub changes lower than the agent-side value, which is what attempt02 recorded (1573 < 1575). The watermark is monotonic, so an agent value higher than a hub-side sample means the agent was already current."
  },
